Negotiations on Beat22 give you the flexibility to close deals your way. Here's how it works for sellers:

### **Negotiation flow:**

-   You can **accept** the buyer's offer anytime.
-   You can also **counter** the offer, change the **price**, **publishing rights**, or **master rights**.
-   You can respond up to **3 rounds** (offer & counter).

![You can respond up to 3 rounds (offer & counter).](/images/2025/06/Screenshot-2025-06-30-235611.png)

![You can respond up to 3 rounds (offer & counter).](/images/2025/06/Screenshot-2025-06-30-235626.png)

### **Ending a negotiation:**

-   After 3 rounds of negotiation, you'll get the option to **Accept** or **Reject**.
-   If you don’t want to proceed further, you can simply reject at this point.

![If you don’t want to proceed further, you can simply reject at this point.](/images/2025/06/Screenshot-2025-06-30-235643.png)

### **Buyer checkout time:**

-   Once you accept an offer, the buyer has **24 hours** to complete the checkout.
-   If they don’t, the negotiation offer will **automatically expire**.

![If they don’t, the negotiation offer will automatically expire.](/images/2025/06/Screenshot-2025-06-30-235658.png)
